ng_hci: refuse an LP_ConnectReq with an unknown link type

ng_hci_lp_con_req() dispatches on the link type ng_l2cap passes in
LP_ConnectReq (ACL, SCO, LE public or LE random) and panicked on any
other value. Log it, free the message and return EINVAL instead.

Origin: NextBSD (nextbsd/nextbsd-kernel#234). Not upstream.
Applies to: releng/15.1 sys/netgraph/bluetooth/hci/ng_hci_ulpi.c

--- a/sys/netgraph/bluetooth/hci/ng_hci_ulpi.c
+++ b/sys/netgraph/bluetooth/hci/ng_hci_ulpi.c
@@ -108,7 +108,15 @@ ng_hci_lp_con_req(ng_hci_unit_p unit, item_p item, hook_p hook)
 	case NG_HCI_LINK_LE_RANDOM:		
 		return (ng_hci_lp_le_con_req(unit, item, hook, link_type));
 	default:
-		panic("%s: link_type invalid.", __func__);
+		/*
+		 * NextBSD: refuse the request instead of panicking
+		 * (nextbsd/nextbsd-kernel#234).
+		 */
+		NG_HCI_ERR(
+"%s: %s - invalid link type=%d\n",
+			__func__, NG_NODE_NAME(unit->node), link_type);
+		NG_FREE_ITEM(item);
+		break;
 	}
 
 	return (EINVAL);
